<h2 id="performance-and-reliability">Performance and Reliability</h2>

<p>Homeware Sense is designed with reliability in mind:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Automatic Failover</strong>: When hardware sensors are unavailable, the system automatically switches to simulated data</li>
  <li><strong>Consistent API</strong>: Regardless of the underlying platform, the API remains consistent</li>
  <li><strong>Error Handling</strong>: Comprehensive error handling and logging for debugging</li>
  <li><strong>Performance Optimized</strong>: Efficient data polling and caching mechanisms</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="security-considerations">Security Considerations</h2>

<p>Security is paramount in smart home integrations:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Local Processing</strong>: All sensor data processing happens locally</li>
  <li><strong>Secure Connections</strong>: Encrypted communication with supported platforms</li>
  <li><strong>Minimal Permissions</strong>: Only necessary permissions requested</li>
  <li><strong>Privacy Preserving</strong>: No data sent to external services without explicit configuration</li>
</ul>

